  "title": "Monochromatic empty triangles",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "If $X \\subseteq {\\mathbb R}^2$ is a finite set of points which is 2-colored, an empty triangle is a set $T \\subseteq X$ with $|T|=3$ so that the convex hull of $T$ is disjoint from $X \\setminus T$. We say that $T$ is monochromatic if all points in $T$ are the same color.\n\nConjecture There exists a fixed constant $c$ with the following property. If $X \\subseteq {\\mathbb R}^2$ is a set of $n$ points in general position which is 2-colored, then it has $\\ge cn^2$ monochromatic empty triangles.",
